        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Maglev, current-driven (MathWorks reproduction).** m*h'' = m*g - alpha*i^2/h^2 with the current as the input. The PID gains are designed at h = 0.05, 0.15 and 0.25 m (crossover 50 rad/s, phase margin 60 deg, Tf = 1 ms) and interpolated over the measured gap (KpTab, KiTab, KdTab). Trim feedforward c_trim*h, prefilter 10/(s + 10) on the 0.15 -> 0.1875 m step at 0.2 s. Ideal is the reference behaviour 900/(s^2 + 42 s + 900) of the prefiltered setpoint, for comparison only. Dist is a force on the ball (F_dist from t_dist, positive downward), off (0 N) by default.",
